    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Build succeeded and the test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I changed to move date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, labelled by the calendar year it ends in \u2014 e.g. dates on/after 1 July 2025 \u2192 `FY26`).\n\n**New helper**\n- `model/FiscalYear.java` \u2014 single source of the rule. `yearOf(LocalDate)` returns the four-digit ending year (`month >= July ? year+1 : year`); `of(Owner)` formats it as `FY<YY>` from the owner's (already business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate`, or `null` when unset.\n\n**`fiscalYear` response field**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `fiscalYear` property (`FY<YY>`) to the Owner schema; the generated `OwnerDto` picks it up.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 added the `fiscalYear` mapping via `FiscalYear.of(owner)`.\n\n**Membership identifier year segment \u2192 fiscal year** (both duplicated sites kept in sync)\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` and `rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 the `-M<YY>` segment now uses `FiscalYear.yearOf(...) % 100` instead of the raw calendar `getYear() % 100`. Updated the openapi description accordingly.\n\n**Tenure \u2192 elapsed fiscal years**\n- `model/MembershipPoints.java` \u2014 replaced the `> 365`-day window with elapsed fiscal years (`FiscalYear.yearOf(now) - FiscalYear.yearOf(registrationDate) >= TENURE_FISCAL_YEARS`, threshold `1`); the tenure bonus now applies once the owner has crossed into a later fiscal year than they registered. Updated the constant, javadoc, and the openapi description.\n\n**Verification**\n- `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The new `coreReturnsFiscalYear` acceptance test passes (audit log confirms a registration adjusted to 2026-09-14 yields `membershipNumber=...-M27`, matching `FY27`).\n\nOne deliberate behaviour change worth flagging, per the spec: because tenure now keys on fiscal-year boundaries rather than a 365-day window, an owner registered e.g. in June and read in August (same calendar span < 365 days but spanning the 1 July boundary) now earns the tenure bonus, whereas one registered in August and read the following June (nearly a year, but same fiscal year) no longer does.\n\nI chose the Australian-style convention (FY labelled by the ending year, matching the repo's Australian holidays/timezones). The only test pins the `FY\\d{2}` format, not the specific year, so if you intended the *starting* year instead, let me know and I'll flip `yearOf`.",
